\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The mean of the whole mesh}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Take #{B=1}. The single block average is the mean of every
mesh value. In \ref{fdip-00BO} only #{p=0} survives, because
#{\sin(\pi p)} vanishes for every nonzero integer #{p}, so the
limit variance is #{1/\mu}. The same value is the variance of
#{\int_0^1 f}, since that integral retains only the constant
mode of #{G}.}
